{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/74147-patching-in-supernatural-merits","id":74147,"title":"Patching in supernatural merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-18T00:12:36-08:00","id":74147,"title":"Patching in supernatural merits","content":"Had a player being this up. Their character has the five dot telekinetic merit and they often roll horribly so their TK goes nuts quite often. They want to make a deal w/ the demon they met in order to lose it. As it's a mortal/supernatural a merit would the demon be able to patch that merit into their cover or would the cover only be remembered as being telekinetic and the demon would be forced to use Legend to back it up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","name":"FallenXanderel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T05:25:37-08:00","id":74213,"title":"","content":"I see no problem with using it as a justification for spending XP on the Merit. If you're using the advanced Cover rules where each Cover has its own Social Merits I see little problem making the TK a part of that specific Cover (although you might have to surrender some of your other Merit dots to make room for the TK). But if you don't spend the XP you have to rely on Legend to &quot;fill in the gaps.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T17:27:46-08:00","id":74664,"title":"","content":"TL;DR - demons can't access supernatural merits with pacts or with legend. Though, as always, remember the golden rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I believe the GMC update has a caveat with the supernatural powers which indicates that anything with a supernatural template cannot have any supernatural merits (they must remain human or they disappear). pg 172<br /> <br /> I believe this is in line with the text in the demon rulebook which states that demons cannot patch in other supernatural's powers (i.e. werewolf shapeshifting, mage spell casting, vampire disciplines) and other such ilk.<br /> <br /> However, I think just plain removing/losing telekinetic powers is doable. Though I think it would be a greater &quot;benefit&quot;. if one wanted to classify losing powers as a &quot;benefit&quot;.<br /> <br /> The sanctity of Merits rule in the GMC (pg 158) would mean that the mortal would gain five free merit dots to allocate somewhere else as the ST allows.<br /> <br /> Anything other non-supernatural thing that the telekinetic wanted to pact with the demon would be dealt with as normal.<br /> <br /> NOTE: even if the demon soul-pacted with the mortal telekinetic and cashed in the pact the demon would not (and should not) gain the telekinetic merit with legend as the pre-requisites of the supernatural merit is, in essence, no supernatural template must be present. Legend requires that the demon meet the prerequisites of the merit on their own or by using legend to attempt to get the pre-requisites. As there is no merit for &quot;counts as having no supernatural template&quot; (and, IMO, there shouldn't be) the demon cannot satisfy the pre-requisites in any way. No telekinesis or other supernatural merit.<br /> <br /> Though, as always, consider your game/ST/group/the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1930,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","user":"Rixx","date":".  Golden Rule 02-18-2014, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T19:07:10-08:00","id":74722,"title":"","content":"Is the Demon and NPC? Than sure. Is anyone playing an Unchained? Probably not.<br /> Can you use a different sort of Demon? Like one from Inferno? Than totally. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T07:46:49-08:00","id":74958,"title":"","content":"RAW, Rixx is correct.<br /> <br /> I tend to speak from my experience with players who like to be slightly special snowflakes, and I'm quite permissive as long as it doesn't kill the group's fun. If, during the course of play, someone wants to &quot;remove the burden of telekinesis&quot; from an NPC or has fixated on the Unseen Sense: Mages Merit, I'm inclined to let them have their fun.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking, it's usually more efficient to buy supernatural powers rather than supernatural merits. They just plain pack a bigger punch for the XP cost. But if you want to buy a big Supernatural Merit instead of new Embed or Exploit, I'm unlikely to stand in your way.<br /> <br /> That said, I've run into players over the years who conflate &quot;this is a reasonable in-game justification for me to have X Merit/power&quot; with &quot;this is a reasonable in-game justification for me to have X Merit/power FOR FREE.&quot; That doesn't fly with me. Twinkery with a narrative explanation is still twinkery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":".  spacing 02-19-2014, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:14:01-08:00","id":75081,"title":"","content":"My players have experimented with only allowing temporary investments of powers like Telepathy - IE, saying to a cultist, 'You have this ability for 24 hours to help us with this mission'. It's a bit of a WP sink but it at least avoids the 'Firestarter' problem and helps cultists make Integrity checks more rarely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T21:12:48-08:00","id":76084,"title":"","content":"The demon is a player, I've suggested Rixx' idea, the loss of the TK was the benifit of the contract and used the SoM clause to allow the player to quickly grasp a fighting style merit tought to them by another PC. In exchange the Demon took a fair bit of the other guys highschool and college life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","name":"FallenXanderel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}